  "Question": "Each pen costs 3 yuan. With 20 yuan, what is the maximum number of pens you can buy? (Give an integer answer.)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "6",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let \\(x\\) be the number of pens purchased. Then \\(3x\\leq20\\), so \\(x\\leq6.67\\). Since \\(x\\) is an integer, the maximum is 6 pens.\n\nAlternative method 1: Use division with remainder\n\nEach pen uses 3 yuan, so divide the budget into groups of 3 yuan:\n\\[\n20=3\\cdot6+2.\n\\]\nThis buys 6 pens and leaves 2 yuan, less than the price of another pen. Therefore the maximum is \\(6\\) pens.",
